-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE SUMMARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SwipeRow is the swipe-to-action row primitive (iOS Mail / Notes style). The web source is a
PURE INTERACTION PRIMITIVE: it wraps `children`, tracks a horizontal touch drag, and on
release either snaps closed, peeks an action open, or auto-fires it. It has NO async data
source — its only "data" hooks are `useIsCoarsePointer` (touch opt-in) and
`useMotionPreference` (reduced-motion). Therefore the generic loading / empty / error /
stale / offline envelopes a data surface carries DO NOT EXIST in this source; reproducing
them would fabricate behavior the web component does not have (a parity violation). The
faithful states — all reproduced and rendered — are the gesture/edge states:
  • inactive passthrough (fine pointer / no actions / disabled) — renders children as-is
  • active idle (closed), dragging, peek-leading, peek-trailing
  • reduced-motion snap collapse ; default(cyan) vs danger(rose) tone
Native binding: motion via @Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion) (the platform P1/S8
preference holder, per Sources/Components/Motion/Motion.swift precedent); coarse-pointer via
the SwipeRowPointerCapability seam; gesture state via the @Observable SwipeRowModel (P1/S8);
telemetry view.opened (slug "SwipeRow") via the SwipeRowTelemetry seam (P1/S11); strings via
the SwipeRowStrings facade (P1/S10). Haptic (web navigator.vibrate(10)) via SwipeRowHaptic.

Files (10): SwipeRow.swift .Adapter .Seams .Model .Views .States .Previews .strings
            .Tests .ModelTests

