WHY THE xcodebuild STEPS ARE BLOCKED (platform / scope evidence — not red, not green)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#1  Central registration is OUT OF SCOPE for this prompt.
    The xcodebuild app/test targets enumerate their Swift sources from `apps/apple/project.yml`
    (paths Sources, TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets, TeslaSync/feature-views). A NEW
    `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` directory must be added there to be compiled. project.yml is
    NOT in this prompt's Allowed Files (Allowed: apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/SwipeRow.*,
    the log) — it is owned by the P4 acceptance gate this surface "Blocks", and editing it from
    a parallel per-surface slot would collide with every sibling slot. Proof (xcodegen generate
    from the unmodified spec):
        SwipeRow refs in generated project.pbxproj      : 0
        shared-surfaces refs in generated project.pbxproj: 0
        feature-views refs (already registered)          : 3
    => even a successful app build would NOT include or test this surface in-scope.

#2  The app/test targets link the KMP core as `Frameworks/Shared.xcframework`, which is ABSENT
    (the staged path holds only .gitkeep). It is assembled by the Kotlin/Native Gradle toolchain
    via the scheme's pre-build "Stage Shared.xcframework" action
    (apps/apple/Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh -> apps/shared/gradlew
    :core:assembleSharedXCFramework). Building the KMP framework is out of scope for a
    shared-surface UI prompt and is not produced in this environment. Real failure captured
    above (exit 65).

Note: Xcode 26.5 + the iPhone 16 simulator ARE present and were exercised (xcodegen generate
EXIT=0; xcodebuild reached the link/dependency phase). The block is the two scope/dependency
